    "https://careers.purdue.edu/PNW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer%2C-Department-of-Mathematics-and-Statistics/38400-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited Term Lecturer, Department of Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Limited Term Lecturer, Department of Mathematics and Statistics Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Search Jobs Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 38400 Job Title: Limited Term Lecturer, Department of Mathematics and Statistics City: Hammond and Westville Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Mathematics and Statistics is seeking applications for a Limited Term Lecturer (LTL) in Statistics. Potential courses include Statistics and Contemporary Life and Elementary Statistical Methods. LTL positions are temporary, non-benefits eligible, part-time positions hired each semester on an as-needed basis. invites applications for part-time positions starting in Fall 2025. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Obligations of this position may include but are not limited to: Meeting with students during and outside of assigned classes Assessing student work and performance Preparing course materials Providing copies of course materials to the department Maintain grades in electronic format Assigning and submitting grades in accordance with established PNW schedules Maintaining FERPA and Title X certification Education Master's Degree in Statistics or a closely related field (minimum 18 hours of graduate work in Statistics) is required Experience Teaching Experience preferred How to Apply Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To apply, applicants should submit the following: A cover letter specifically addressing required experience A curriculum vitae List of three professional references. FLSA Status Exempt Apply now Posting Start Date: 8/7/25 Search Jobs View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2018 Purdue University Northwest | An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/PNW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer%2C-English/38157-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited Term Lecturer, English",
      "description": "Limited Term Lecturer, English Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Search Jobs Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 38157 Job Title: Limited Term Lecturer, English City: Hammond Job Description: Job Summary The Department of English and World Languages is seeking applications for Limited Term Lecturers (LTLs) in English.  LTL positions are temporary, non-benefits eligible, part-time positions hired each semester on an as-needed basis. The Primary Responsibilities of successful candidates will be to: Teach on campus and/or online courses in introductory English courses Follow the syllabus and curricula provided. Maintain office hours and provide feedback to students in a timely manner. Maintain FERPA and Title X certification Assist with program-related duties and administrative tasks, including placement, orientation, proctoring, student evaluations, curriculum and program review Understand and adhere to University policies and guidelines Have competency in effective and appropriate online (synchronous and asynchronous) delivery and in-person instruction Education Master’s degree in English or a related field (minimum 18 hours of graduate work in English) Experience Demonstrated experience teaching at the college level or relevant professional experience Core Competencies Strong interpersonal, presentation, and written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated ability to communicate both orally and in writing in English University Overview Purdue University Northwest (PNW) Purdue University Northwest (PNW), a premier metropolitan university located in Northwest Indiana, is dedicated to empowering transformational change in its students on its two campuses in Hammond and Westville, Indiana. Part of the Purdue University system and offering more than 70 undergraduate and graduate degree programs, PNW is committed to academic excellence, supports growth, and celebrates diversity. PNW’s colleges, schools and centers are distinguished through prestigious accreditations, national recognitions, and competitive rankings. PNW’s Hammond campus is located only 30 miles from Chicago with the Westville branch campus just 15 miles from the Indiana Dunes National Park. Fostering a university community full of contrasts—urban and rural, industrial and natural, with a well-established history and forward-thinking mindset—PNW’s two campuses serve its students, many of whom are the first in their families to attend college to make the most of this rich range of resources. Moreover, PNW has been designated as a Hispanic-serving public institution dedicated to excellence in teaching and learning and committed to the advancement of a diverse and under-served student population. College Profile The College of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and 250 graduate students across a wide range of programs. The College also houses the Community Counseling Center that provides quality affordable mental health services and the Institute for Social and Policy Research, which uses social science and policy analysis methods to find solutions to educational, social, and health-related challenges facing the citizens of Northwest Indiana and the Chicago metropolitan region. The college is also home to the Willie T. Donald Exoneration Advisory Coalition to support those who have been wrongfully convicted in the state of Indiana. FLSA Status Exempt Apply now Posting Start Date: 7/21/25 Search Jobs View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2018 Purdue University Northwest | An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/PNW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer-Nursing/12358-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited Term Lecturer - Nursing",
      "description": "Limited Term Lecturer - Nursing Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Search Jobs Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 12358 Job Title: Limited Term Lecturer - Nursing City: Hammond/Westville Job Description: Job Summary Grow your career in the country's most trusted profession by joining Purdue University Northwest College of Nursing, a designated NLN Center of Nursing Excellence.  PNW provides high quality affordable undergraduate and graduate education to students of Northwest Indiana and beyond.  PNW College of Nursing maintains a commitment to quality, evidence-based nursing education and has a reputation for clinical excellence.  We promote critical inquiry through experiential learning, faculty scholarships, civic engagement and community partnerships.  If you are an experienced RN with a least a master's degree in nursing and you share these attributes, we invite you to consider a position as a Limited Term Lecturer. College Overview PNW offers the following programs: Undergraduate BSN - Professional BSN - Accelerated Bachelor's Second Degree BSN - Online RNBSN Graduate MSN - Nurse Executive - Online MSN - Nursing Educator - Online MSN - Family Nurse Practitioner MSN - Adult Gerontology Clinical Nurse Speciality Post-Master's Certificate - Adult Gerontology Clinical Nurse Specialist Post-Master's Certificate - Family Nurse Practitioner Post-Master's Certificate - Nursing Education DNP Education Excellent candidates  at a minimum, will possess the following qualifications: Master’s Degree in Nursing for undergraduate teaching opportunities DNP or PhD required for graduate level opportunities Certification in program area preferred Exceptional, experienced based subject matter expertise Excellent written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated teaching or precepting experience Commitment to life-long learning and eagerness to serve students Additional Information Limited Term Lecturer (LTL) positions are temporary, non-benefits eligible, part-time positions hired each semester on an as-needed basis.  LTL's provide instruction for nursing students in collaboration with the College's fulltime faculty.  All nursing faculty members are expected to be dedicated to excellence in nursing education, be actively engaged in nursing scholarship, and possess un unencumbered licensure as a Registered Professional Nurse in the state of instruction and Indiana or a multistate compact license. Applicants interested in undergraduate courses should send CV/Resume and preferred area of interest statement to mschallm@pnw.edu for consideration.  Applicants interested in graduate courses or supervision should send their CV/Resume and prefered area of interest statement to teastlan@pnw.edu Purdue University is an EEO/AA employer. Experience 0 FLSA Status Exempt Apply now Posting Start Date: 4/17/24 Search Jobs View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2018 Purdue University Northwest | An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/PNW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer%2C-Department-of-Biological-Sciences/16790-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited Term Lecturer, Department of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Limited Term Lecturer, Department of Biological Sciences Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Search Jobs Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 16790 Job Title: Limited Term Lecturer, Department of Biological Sciences City: Hammond and Westville Job Description: Job Summary The Biology Department invites applications for part-time positions starting in Fall 2022 teaching in-person laboratories in the Biological Sciences on the Hammond and Westville Campuses. Potential courses include Anatomy and Physiology, Microbiology, Introductory Biology and courses for non-science majors. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Obligations of this position may include but are not limited to: •    meeting with students during and outside of assigned classes, •    assessing student work and performance, •    preparing course materials, •    providing copies of course materials to the department •    maintain grades in electronic format •    assigning and submitting grades in accordance with established PNW schedules •    maintaining FERPA  and Title X certification Education Master's Degree in Biological Sciences or related M.S. or Professional Degree required Experience Teaching Experience preferred FLSA Status Exempt Apply now Posting Start Date: 5/31/22 Search Jobs View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2018 Purdue University Northwest | An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/PNW/job/Professor-Assistant/44193-en_US": {
      "title": "Professor Assistant",
      "description": "Professor Assistant Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Search Jobs Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 44193 Job Title: Professor Assistant City: Hammond Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Engineering Technology at Purdue University Northwest invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position with a 9-month academic appointment at the Assistant Professor level in the fields of Electrical/Electronics and/or Robotics and Automation. The position will support strategic focus areas of the College of Technology within robotics, automation, and intelligent systems, with applications across Electrical Engineering Technology and Mechatronics Engineering Technology. Qualifications Doctoral degree in electrical or electronics engineering or technology, or a related discipline, is required by the start of employment. Effective communication skills are required. Relevant, recent industrial experience or prior teaching experience is highly desirable. Undergraduate degree must be in a relevant area. Documentation of classroom effectiveness, external engagement, or related activities is preferred. Responsibilities Teach and develop graduate and undergraduate courses in areas such as robotics, industrial automation, programmable logic controllers (PLCs), process control, mechatronics, and related areas. Develop an independent, externally funded research program aligned with the candidate’s expertise and the strategic direction of the department. Support graduate students through sustained research activity. Participate in industrial engagement and various committees. Interacting with regional businesses are encouraged. Engage undergraduate and graduate students in applied research. The applied research portfolio of the Department of Engineering Technology crosses the disciplines of mechatronics and electrical and computer engineering technology, with focus areas in materials, design, robotics, automation, smart manufacturing, digital twins, and additive manufacturing. The Department of Engineering Technology offers full support when presenting peer review papers at conferences. The department and the university offer several internal opportunities for professional development and for external grant application preparation. Department Profile The Department of Engineering Technology is housed at the Hammond, Indiana, campus, and the Engineering Technology programs are accredited by the Technology Accreditation Commission of ABET. The department also offers master’s and doctoral programs through the College of Technology Graduate Studies. University Profile Purdue University Northwest (PNW), is a student-centered university located in Northwest Indiana, is dedicated to empowering transformational change in its students on its two campuses in Hammond and Westville, Indiana. Part of the Purdue University system and offering more than 60 undergraduate and graduate degree programs, PNW is committed to academic excellence and supports growth. PNW’s colleges, schools, and centers are distinguished through prestigious accreditations, national recognitions, and competitive rankings. PNW’s Hammond campus is located only 30 miles from Chicago with the Westville branch campus just 15 miles from the Indiana Dunes National Park. Fostering a university community full of contrasts – urban and rural, industrial and natural, with a well-established history and forward-thinking mindset – PNW’s two campuses serve its students, many of whom are the first in their families to attend college to make the most of this rich range of resources. Application Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted electronically on the PNW Careers Faculty webpage. A complete application package will include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Professional References Unofficial Transcript Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Additional Information Questions may be sent to Search Chair at ecet@pnw.edu . Visit our website www.pnw.edu for additional information about the university. For information regarding our excellent benefits package, visit www.purdue.edu/benefits . Employment is contingent upon completion of successful background check. Purdue University Northwest is an equal opportunity/equal access university. FLSA Status Exempt Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/19/26 Search Jobs View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2018 Purdue University Northwest | An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    },
    "https://careers.purdue.edu/PNW/job/Limited-Term-Lecturer%2C-Communication/37155-en_US": {
      "title": "Limited Term Lecturer, Communication",
      "description": "Limited Term Lecturer, Communication Job Details | Purdue University By continuing to use and navigate this website, you are agreeing to the use of cookies. Accept Close Skip to main content Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Search Jobs Home Page Internal Applicants View Jobs Faculty Staff Student Language English (United States) View Profile Employee Login Search Jobs Job Description Apply now Req Id: 37155 Job Title: Limited Term Lecturer, Communication City: Hammond Job Description: Job Summary The Department of Communication & Creative Arts is seeking applications for Limited Term Lecturers (LTLs) in English.  LTL positions are temporary, non-benefits eligible, part-time positions hired each semester on an as-needed basis. The Primary Responsibilities of successful candidates will be to: Teach on campus and/or online courses in introductory Communications courses; including public speaking Follow the syllabus and curricula provided. Maintain office hours and provide feedback to students in a timely manner. Maintain FERPA and Title X certification Assist with program-related duties and administrative tasks, including placement, orientation, proctoring, student evaluations, curriculum and program review Understand and adhere to University policies and guidelines Have competency in effective and appropriate online (synchronous and asynchronous) delivery and in-person instruction Education, Experience, Training and/or Certifications Master’s degree in Communication or a related field (minimum 18 hours of graduate work in Communications) Strong interpersonal, presentation, and written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated experience teaching at the college level or relevant professional experience Demonstrated ability to communicate both orally and in writing in English University Overview Purdue University Northwest (PNW), is a premier metropolitan university dedicated to empowering transformational change in our students and in our community. PNW serves approximately 9,300 students across two campuses, offering more than 70 areas of student at the baccalaureate, masters, and doctoral levels. Located in Northwest Indiana, near Chicago, PNW values academic excellence, supports growth, and celebrates diversity. College Profile The College of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences serves over 1,500 undergraduate students and 250 graduate students across a wide range of programs. The College also houses the Community Counseling Center that provides quality affordable mental health services and the Institute for Social and Policy Research, which uses social science and policy analysis methods to find solutions to educational, social, and health-related challenges facing the citizens of Northwest Indiana and the Chicago metropolitan region. The college is also home to the Willie T. Donald Exoneration Advisory Coalition to support those who have been wrongfully convicted in the state of Indiana. How to Apply Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To apply, applicants should submit the following: 1) a cover letter specifically addressing required experience; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) list of three professional references. A background check will be required for employment in this position. Employment would begin on August 11, 2025 and continue on an annual basis. Purdue University Northwest is committed to advancing diversity in all areas of faculty effort, including scholarship, instruction, and engagement. Candidates should address at least one of these areas in their cover letter, indicating their experiences, current interests or activities, and/or future goals to promote a climate that values diversity and inclusion. Purdue University is an equal opportunity/equal access/affirmative action employer fully committed to achieving a diverse workforce. All individuals, including minorities, woman, individuals with disabilities, and protected veterans are encouraged to apply. FLSA Status Exempt Apply now Posting Start Date: 10/28/26 Search Jobs View All Jobs Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. © 2018 Purdue University Northwest | An equal access/equal opportunity university"
    }
  },
